        <h2 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 10px;">3 Mounting</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5;">Anchoring the MBC must be accomplished following all national, state and local codes.</p>

        <h3 style="font-size: 18pt; margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 10px;">3.1 Anchoring the MBC</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5;">The MBC rests on four pedestal feet (behind kick plates) and each location is pre-drilled for attaching the unit to floor. The holes on the long sides are <span data-field="dimension_long_side">{{ dimension_long_side }}</span> apart and the holes on the short sides are <span data-field="dimension_short_side">{{ dimension_short_side }}</span> apart.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5;">Figure 3-1 shows the location of the anchoring holes. Also note in the figure, the unit has pre-cut openings for input or output cables. Figure 2-2. Clearances shows to the opening on the top of the unit for cables.</p>

